# Always push to GitHub

After completing substantive code or content changes in this project:

1. Commit the relevant files with a concise message.
2. Push to `origin` (`main`) without waiting for a separate request.
3. Report the result briefly (commit done / pushed).

Do not skip push unless the user explicitly says not to push, or GitHub auth/network blocks it (then say so).
